Question 4: Maximum Task Window Within Budget (Variable-Size Sliding Window) 
Riya is scheduling a pipeline of processes on an embedded processor. Each process 𝑖 has a known energy cost arr[i]. The processor has a strict power limit 𝑃 for any contiguous execution sequence. Riya wants to find the maximum number of consecutive tasks she can execute without their combined energy cost exceeding the limit 𝑃. 
She uses a variable-size sliding window: 
1.	Maintain a start pointer at index 0 and a running sum of energy current_sum. 
2.	Iterate an end pointer from 0 to N - 1 and add arr[end] to current_sum. 
3.	If current_sum exceeds 𝑃,increment start and subtract arr[start] from current_sum until current_sum <= P. 
4.	Keep track of the maximum window size (end - start + 1) encountered during the process. 
•	The first line of input consists of two space-separated integers: 𝑁 (the number of tasks) and 𝑃 (the maximum allowed energy consumption). 
•	The second line of input consists of 𝑁 space-separated positive integers representing the energy costs of the tasks. 
•	Print a single integer representing the maximum consecutive tasks in the format: Max Length: 
X. 
•	1 ≤ 𝑁 ≤ 10000 
•	1 ≤ 𝑎𝑟𝑟[𝑖] ≤ 104 
•	1 ≤ 𝑃 ≤ 108 
Input 1: codeText 
5 8 
3	1 2 4 5 
Output 1: codeText Max Length: 3 Input 2: codeText 
4	5 
6 7 8 9 
Output 2: codeText 
Max Length: 0 

Aim

To write a C program to find the maximum number of consecutive elements whose sum is less than or equal to the given limit using the sliding window method.

Pseudocode

Start
Read N and P
Read the array elements
start = 0
sum = 0
max = 0
For end = 0 to N - 1
sum = sum + array[end]
While sum > P
sum = sum - array[start]
start = start + 1
If (end - start + 1) > max
max = end - start + 1
Print "Max Length:", max
End

C Program Code

#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    int n, p;
    int arr[100];
    int i;
    int start = 0;
    int end;
    int sum = 0;
    int max = 0;
    int size;
    printf("Enter the number of elements and limit: ");
    scanf("%d %d", &n, &p);
    printf("Enter the array elements:\n");
    for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        scanf("%d", &arr[i]);
    }
    for(end = 0; end < n; end++)
    {
        sum = sum + arr[end];
        while(sum > p)
        {
            sum = sum - arr[start];
            start = start + 1;
        }
        size = end - start + 1;
        if(size > max)
        {
            max = size;
        }
    }
    printf("Max Length: %d", max);
    return 0;
}

