Question 5: Sliding Window Maximum Peak (Monotonic Window Queue) 
Rohan is building a real-time graphics rendering system. The system receives a sequence of frame rendering times. To smooth out frame drops, Rohan must calculate the peak (maximum) rendering time in every sliding window of 𝐾 consecutive frames. 
To achieve an optimal 𝑂(𝑁) runtime, Rohan uses a monotonic double-ended queue (deque) to store indices of elements in the sliding window: 
1.	As the window slides from left to right, maintain the deque such that indices of elements are stored in decreasing order of their corresponding values. 
2.	For each element arr[i]: 
o	Remove indices from the back of the deque if their corresponding values are less than or equal to the current element arr[i] (they can no longer be the maximum). 
o	Insert the current index i at the back of the deque. 
o	Remove the index from the front of the deque if it falls outside the bounds of the current sliding window (i.e., if the index is less than i - K + 1). 
3.	For every step where the window is fully formed (when i >= K - 1), the element at the index stored at the front of the deque is the maximum for that window. 
Note: Since standard C does not have a built-in deque, you can implement a basic deque using a preallocated array of size 𝑁 with front and rear pointer indices. 
•	The first line of input consists of two space-separated integers: 𝑁 (the total number of frames) and 𝐾 (the sliding window size). 
•	The second line of input consists of 𝑁 space-separated integers representing the frame rendering times. 
•	Print a single line of space-separated integers representing the maximum value for each sliding window of size 𝐾. 
•	1 ≤ 𝐾 ≤ 𝑁 ≤ 10000 
•	−105 ≤ 𝑎𝑟𝑟[𝑖] ≤ 105 
Input 1: codeText 
8 3 
1 3 -1 -3 5 3 6 7 Output 1: codeText 
3 3 5 5 6 7 Input 2: codeText 
4 2 
4 3 2 1 
Output 2: codeText 
4 3 2 

Aim

To write a C program to find the maximum element in every sliding window of size K.

Pseudocode 

Start
Read N and K
Read the array elements
For i = 0 to N - K
max = array[i]
For j = i + 1 to i + K - 1
If array[j] > max
max = array[j]
Print max
End

C Program Code

